+### Task 4: A failing file is retried, then poisoned
+
+On a `FileError` the file's work is rolled back and its marker records one more failure; at
+`POISON_AFTER` failures the marker is `poisoned` and later runs skip it without opening it (§4.7,
+§6.1). `run` reports each file that failed or was poisoned this run through a callback, so the
+command line (Task 5) can write its stderr line without `run` knowing about streams.
